# Project: YorùbáOCR Research

## What this project is
A benchmark dataset + fine-tuning study for Yorùbá OCR submitted to
Deep Learning Indaba 2026 (IJCAI volume). The **primary supervised model**
is **PaddleOCR-VL-1.5** (LoRA fine-tuned on Yorùbá line crops); PaddleOCR
PP-OCRv4 fine-tuning remains a classical CRNN comparison and the target of
scripted ablations. The researcher built a custom annotation platform
(yoruba-ocr.vercel.app) and exported data in PaddleOCR line-crop format.

## Verified dataset facts (do not invent alternatives)
- Source: Yorùbá di Wúrà Book Series (printed books, 2021)
- Language: Standard Yorùbá, corrected=yes for all entries
- Format: line crops (PNG) + tab-separated label files (PaddleOCR format)
  - Each label line: images/{split}/hash_lineNNNN.png<TAB>ground_truth_text
- 25+ independent annotation export batches in data/raw/
- Approximate totals after consolidation + hygiene: 2,945 unique lines
  (80/10/10 line-level split with `--resplit --seed 42`: 2,356 train /
  294 val / 295 test; reported Table 1 metrics use prior n=326 test export)
- Character dictionary: built from consolidated labels (currently **99** graphemes excl. space on disk; varies with hygiene)
- Metadata columns: image, text, source, year, dialect, corrected, parent_image, line_index
- Consolidated data lives in data/processed/ after running 01_consolidate_data.py

## Pipeline scripts (in execution order)
1. scripts/01_consolidate_data.py  — merge exports, deduplicate, copy to data/processed/
2. scripts/02_analyze_dataset.py   — EDA: char/diacritic distribution, text length stats
3. scripts/03_generate_config.py   — download pretrained weights + write fine-tune YAML
4. scripts/04_train_paddleocr.py   — PP-OCRv4 CRNN fine-tuning (comparison + ablations; needs PaddleOCR repo)
5. scripts/05_evaluate.py          — CER/WER/DER evaluation for any model
6. scripts/06_baseline_pretrained.py — English pretrained PP-OCR eval (via 05)
7. scripts/09_baseline_qwen.py, scripts/10_ablation_study.py — optional Qwen / PP-OCRv4 ablations
8. scripts/11_compile_results.py   — paper tables from metrics.csv
9. **PaddleOCR-VL-1.5 (HF) — main supervised track:** scripts/14–16 + adapter eval (15)
10. scripts/17–19 — stratified DER, DER-universe, bootstrap CIs
11. **OOTB baselines (Section A):** `22_evaluate_trocr.py` (zero-shot), `20_baseline_surya_v2.py`
12. **Fine-tuned (Section B):** VL-1.5 LoRA (16); TrOCR (`21–22` via `phase_21_trocr.sh`); optional Surya Foundation (`26–28`)
13. **Hub release:** `25_upload_hf_dataset.py`, `29_upload_hf_models.py`
14. **Run hygiene:** scripts/metrics_lifecycle.py, scripts/02c_refresh_dataset_report.py

## Models being compared
1. PaddleOCR-VL-1.5 (Hugging Face) — zero-shot + **LoRA fine-tuned (primary supervised)**; scripts 14–16
2. PaddleOCR PP-OCRv4 English pretrained — baseline (`05_evaluate.py`)
3. PaddleOCR PP-OCRv4 CRNN fine-tuned — classical comparison + ablation target (`04`, `10`)
4. TrOCR-large-printed — zero-shot (`22` + `--pretrained-model-id`); **fine-tuned in Section B** (`21–22`)
5. Surya v2 — zero-shot recognition on line crops (`20`); optional Surya Foundation fine-tune (`26–28`)
6. Qwen 2.5 VL — zero-shot multimodal (`09`, optional)

## Metrics
- CER — Character Error Rate (NFC-normalised edit distance / gt char count)
- WER — Word Error Rate (NFC-normalised word-level edit distance / gt word count)
- DER — Diacritic Error Rate (novel contribution):
    pred_diacs = [c for c in NFD(pred) if unicodedata.combining(c)]
    gt_diacs   = [c for c in NFD(gt)   if unicodedata.combining(c)]
    DER = edit_distance(pred_diacs, gt_diacs) / len(gt_diacs)
  Measures tone mark and subdot fidelity specifically — the key failure mode
  of English pretrained models on Yorùbá text.

## All results must be traceable
- Every number in the paper must map to an entry in results/tables/metrics.csv
- Per-sample JSONL logs are written alongside every eval run
- Never write a metric value in prose that is not in results/tables/

## Terminology: always use these exact forms
- Yorùbá (with diacritics, never "Yoruba")
- diacritic minimal pairs (not "similar characters")
- toneme, tonograph, combining diacritic
- low-resource (hyphenated when modifier)
- fine-tuning (hyphenated)
- CER, WER, DER (always capitalised)

